{"10":[{"k":"p","t":"OPERATOR OPTIONAL SWITCH SETTINGS"},{"k":"p","t":"The option switches are located on the CPU Board. The option switches and audio control can be reached through the back of the machine."},{"k":"p","t":"The following table will assist your adjustments:"},{"k":"p","t":"OPTIONAL SWITCH SETTINGS"},{"k":"p","t":"Switch 1 controls the number of cars alloted each player per game. The switch settings should be as follows:"},{"k":"p","t":"SWITCH 1: NUMBER OF CARS: OFF 3 On 5"},{"k":"p","t":"Switches 2 and 3 are not used."},{"k":"p","t":"Switches 4 and 5 control the game fees. These settings can be set for one coin (25\u00a2) or two coins (50\u00a2) per play as follows:"},{"k":"tr","t":"SWITCH 4:   SWITCH 5:   COIN SETTING:"},{"k":"tr","t":"OFF   OFF   One Coin (25\u00a2) - One Play"},{"k":"tr","t":"ON   OFF   Two Coins(50\u00a2) - One Play"},{"k":"p","t":"Switch 6 is a preset factory adjustment, and should remain in the \"ON\" position for the video upright game."},{"k":"p","t":"Switch 7 is preset at the factory, and should be set in the \"ON\" position for the monitor picture adjustment."},{"k":"p","t":"Switch 8 allows the operator to regulate the availability of music in the attract mode. The following settings regulate this function:"},{"k":"p","t":"SWITCH 8: ATTRACT MODE MUSIC: ON Music Available OFF Music Not Available"}],"12":[{"k":"p","t":"ROM _A6 PRINTED CIRCUIT BOARD #50330010"},{"k":"p","t":"PARTS LIST"},{"k":"p","t":"NO. PART NUMBER: DESCRIPTION: USAGE:"},{"k":"tr","t":"1   50010306   MB8841   1"},{"k":"tr","t":"2   50010264LS   74LS368   3"},{"k":"tr","t":"3   50010105LS   74LS32   1"},{"k":"tr","t":"4   50010139LS   74LS175   1"},{"k":"tr","t":"5   50040002   -l mfd, 50 Volt Ceramic Disc Cap. 3"},{"k":"tr","t":"6   50040141   .00lmfd, 50 V., Ceramic Disc Cap. 1"},{"k":"tr","t":"7   50040170   220PF, 50 V., Ceramic Disc Cap.   1"},{"k":"tr","t":"8   50060178   4.7mfd, 10 V. Tantalum Capacitor 1"},{"k":"tr","t":"9   50100014   1N914 Diode   1"